More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (701–710)
701. Improper Validation of Two-Factor Authentication Tokens
Two-Factor Authentication Bypass
Attackers bypass two-factor authentication due to weak token validation.
💰 Typical payout: $800 – $12,000
702. Insecure Handling of API Request Caching
Sensitive API Cache Exposure
Sensitive API responses are cached and served to unauthorized users.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
703. Improper Validation of Password Recovery Questions
Security Question Authentication Weakness
Weak or predictable recovery questions allow attackers to reset accounts.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
704. Insecure Handling of File Compression Services
Archive Processing Vulnerability
File compression or extraction services allow malicious archive exploitation.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
705. Improper Validation of API Authentication Parameters
Authentication Parameter Manipulation
Attackers modify authentication parameters to bypass login verification.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
706. Insecure Handling of WebSocket Authentication
WebSocket Authentication Bypass
WebSocket connections allow unauthorized users to connect without proper authentication.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
707. Improper Validation of User Notification Settings
Notification Settings Authorization Bypass
Users modify notification settings belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
708. Insecure Handling of Cloud Instance Metadata
Cloud Metadata Exposure
Cloud metadata endpoints reveal sensitive credentials or internal information.
💰 Typical payout: $1,000 – $15,000
709. Improper Validation of Resource Sharing Links
Resource Sharing Link Guessing
Attackers guess or reuse sharing links to access private resources.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
710. Insecure Handling of API Response Compression
Compression Side-Channel Attack
Improper compression handling allows attackers to infer sensitive data.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
